# Commit messages (Source Control “Generate” button)

When generating a Git commit message for this repository:

- Use Conventional Commits: `type: short summary`
- Allowed types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `perf`, `style`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `build`, `ci`
- One line only — subject ≤ 72 characters
- Imperative mood (“add”, “fix”, “refactor”) — not “added” / “fixed”
- No body, no bullet lists, no explanations of the diff
- No trailing period
- Prefer scope only when obvious: `feat(dashboard): …`

Examples:
- `feat: promote streak in dashboard hero`
- `fix: align hero sky to bottom-right`
- `refactor: defer recurring task sync after response`
- `perf: code-split focus timer and analytics charts`
- `chore: update loading skeletons`
